      "text": "4. Constrained Masking & Greedy Selection",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4. Constrained Masking & Greedy Selection",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "e4794910-adc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2130,
      "y": 248,
      "width": 424.08,
      "height": 259.20000000000005,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#052e16",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 41831,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Interception Point (Before Token Selection):\n\u2022 Standard LLM: next_id = argmax(z) or sample(Softmax(z))\n\u2022 Constrained Decoding: overwrite invalid logits with -\u221e:\n\n  z_masked[i] = z[i]     if token i is schema-legal\n  z_masked[i] = -inf     if token i is illegal\n\nMathematical Guarantee:\n\u2022 exp(-inf) = 0  =>  P(illegal token) = 0.0\n\u2022 Because exp(z) is monotonic, argmax(z_masked) equals\n  argmax(Softmax(z_masked)) without computing exp().\n\nAutoregressive Feedback Loop:\n\u2022 Append next_id to input_ids -> repeat T+1.\n\u2022 Model's own learned weights decide among valid tokens;\n  grammar rules make invalid tokens impossible.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Interception Point (Before Token Selection):\n\u2022 Standard LLM: next_id = argmax(z) or sample(Softmax(z))\n\u2022 Constrained Decoding: overwrite invalid logits with -\u221e:\n\n  z_masked[i] = z[i]     if token i is schema-legal\n  z_masked[i] = -inf     if token i is illegal\n\nMathematical Guarantee:\n\u2022 exp(-inf) = 0  =>  P(illegal token) = 0.0\n\u2022 Because exp(z) is monotonic, argmax(z_masked) equals\n  argmax(Softmax(z_masked)) without computing exp().\n\nAutoregressive Feedback Loop:\n\u2022 Append next_id to input_ids -> repeat T+1.\n\u2022 Model's own learned weights decide among valid tokens;\n  grammar rules make invalid tokens impossible.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
