      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Byte-Level BPE & The 256-Byte Bijection (bytes_to_unicode)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Byte-Level BPE & The 256-Byte Bijection (bytes_to_unicode)",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "eaeefa62-453",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 758,
      "width": 892.8,
      "height": 259.20000000000005,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#451a03",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 31919,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Subject Bonus Rule (Page 18): Avoid direct use of model.encode() and model.decode() in main code;\nrely ONLY on get_logits_from_input_ids() and get_path_to_vocab_file().\n\nWhy Byte-Level BPE Maps Bytes to Printable Unicode:\n\u2022 JSON strings in vocab.json cannot cleanly store raw control bytes (0x00..0x1F) or arbitrary UTF-8 bytes.\n\u2022 GPT-2 / Qwen defines a lossless 1-to-1 bijection between all 256 byte values (0..255) and 256 printable\n  Unicode codepoints:\n  - Printable ASCII & Latin-1 bytes (33..126, 161..172, 174..255) map to chr(b) directly.\n  - Control bytes & whitespace (0..32, 127..160, 173) map to chr(256 + n):\n      * Byte 0x20 (space ' ') -> chr(256 + 32) = chr(288) = '\u0120'  (e.g. '\u0120sum' = b' sum')\n      * Byte 0x0A (newline '\\n') -> chr(256 + 10) = chr(266) = '\u010a'\n\nHow to Build Custom decode(token_ids) from vocab.json:\n  1. Load vocab.json: str_to_id = json.load(f)  ->  invert: id_to_str = {v: k for k, v in str_to_id.items()}\n  2. Build reverse map unicode_to_byte: dict[str, int] (all 256 entries).\n  3. For token_ids: concat strings -> map each char via unicode_to_byte -> bytes(...).decode('utf-8', errors='replace').",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Subject Bonus Rule (Page 18): Avoid direct use of model.encode() and model.decode() in main code;\nrely ONLY on get_logits_from_input_ids() and get_path_to_vocab_file().\n\nWhy Byte-Level BPE Maps Bytes to Printable Unicode:\n\u2022 JSON strings in vocab.json cannot cleanly store raw control bytes (0x00..0x1F) or arbitrary UTF-8 bytes.\n\u2022 GPT-2 / Qwen defines a lossless 1-to-1 bijection between all 256 byte values (0..255) and 256 printable\n  Unicode codepoints:\n  - Printable ASCII & Latin-1 bytes (33..126, 161..172, 174..255) map to chr(b) directly.\n  - Control bytes & whitespace (0..32, 127..160, 173) map to chr(256 + n):\n      * Byte 0x20 (space ' ') -> chr(256 + 32) = chr(288) = '\u0120'  (e.g. '\u0120sum' = b' sum')\n      * Byte 0x0A (newline '\\n') -> chr(256 + 10) = chr(266) = '\u010a'\n\nHow to Build Custom decode(token_ids) from vocab.json:\n  1. Load vocab.json: str_to_id = json.load(f)  ->  invert: id_to_str = {v: k for k, v in str_to_id.items()}\n  2. Build reverse map unicode_to_byte: dict[str, int] (all 256 entries).\n  3. For token_ids: concat strings -> map each char via unicode_to_byte -> bytes(...).decode('utf-8', errors='replace').",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
