      "text": "3. Subject Rules & Defense Verification Checklist",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. Subject Rules & Defense Verification Checklist",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "b611bf20-c7d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 758,
      "width": 632.4,
      "height": 275.40000000000003,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#450a0a",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 70150,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Hard Subject Prohibitions (Ch. IV.3.1 \u2014 Instant Fail if Violated):\n\u2022 FORBIDDEN imports in your code: torch, transformers, huggingface_hub,\n  outlines, dspy, or any third-party constrained decoding library.\n\u2022 ALLOWED packages: Python stdlib (json, math, argparse, pathlib), numpy,\n  pydantic, and llm_sdk.\n\u2022 FORBIDDEN: Calling any private (_prefixed) attributes/methods on Small_LLM_Model.\n\u2022 FORBIDDEN: Heuristic function selection (e.g. 'if \"sum\" in prompt').\n\u2022 FORBIDDEN: Committing data/output/ directory to Git.\n\nMust-Pass Defense Questions on LLM & Tokenizer Theory:\n1. 'How does a Transformer predict the next token?' -> Embeddings + RoPE ->\n   N layers of Causal Self-Attention + Residual + SwiGLU MLP -> LM Head -> Logits.\n2. 'Why does causal masking matter?' -> Prevents token t from attending to >t.\n3. 'Why -inf instead of -100?' -> Softmax(-inf) = 0; -100 can win if others are -200.\n4. 'Why decode->re-encode in pipeline?' -> BPE merges depend on adjacent context;\n   concatenating raw IDs creates out-of-distribution token boundaries.\n5. 'How do you handle spaces in vocab.json?' -> Byte-level BPE maps 0x20 to '\u0120'.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Hard Subject Prohibitions (Ch. IV.3.1 \u2014 Instant Fail if Violated):\n\u2022 FORBIDDEN imports in your code: torch, transformers, huggingface_hub,\n  outlines, dspy, or any third-party constrained decoding library.\n\u2022 ALLOWED packages: Python stdlib (json, math, argparse, pathlib), numpy,\n  pydantic, and llm_sdk.\n\u2022 FORBIDDEN: Calling any private (_prefixed) attributes/methods on Small_LLM_Model.\n\u2022 FORBIDDEN: Heuristic function selection (e.g. 'if \"sum\" in prompt').\n\u2022 FORBIDDEN: Committing data/output/ directory to Git.\n\nMust-Pass Defense Questions on LLM & Tokenizer Theory:\n1. 'How does a Transformer predict the next token?' -> Embeddings + RoPE ->\n   N layers of Causal Self-Attention + Residual + SwiGLU MLP -> LM Head -> Logits.\n2. 'Why does causal masking matter?' -> Prevents token t from attending to >t.\n3. 'Why -inf instead of -100?' -> Softmax(-inf) = 0; -100 can win if others are -200.\n4. 'Why decode->re-encode in pipeline?' -> BPE merges depend on adjacent context;\n   concatenating raw IDs creates out-of-distribution token boundaries.\n5. 'How do you handle spaces in vocab.json?' -> Byte-level BPE maps 0x20 to '\u0120'.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
